    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Short Riders Rental Paperwork Questions</h1>
    <p>Paperwork is the least glamorous part of renting a motorbike in Hanoi and the part most worth doing well, and for a short rider it carries one extra duty: it is where the fit conversation gets recorded. The questions asked before signing, about condition, deposits, documents and what happens if anything changes, are the same for every rider, but a rider whose machine is borderline-tall has one more reason to ask them clearly, because the paperwork minutes are the last moment when a seat that feels high can still become a seat that was swapped for a better one, free of charge in every sense except two minutes.</p>
    <p>The page sits in the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster and is written for short riders. Verified rental prices are on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, the general question bank is on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, the step-by-step walkthrough is on <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/how-to-rent-a-motorbike-in-hanoi/">how to rent a motorbike in Hanoi</a>, and the money-side conversation lives on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/motorbike-rental-deposit-hanoi/">motorbike rental deposit</a> page.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Why the questions matter more than the answers</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">The condition record, photos before signatures</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">The deposit conversation, asked plainly</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">Licenses, asked and not assumed</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">Insurance and liability, the honest question</a></li>
